title: Customize a Table with Multiline Content
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Building on [[Customize a Table]]: if your cells contain a paragraph (or multiple paragraphs) instead of a single line, the cell markers need `mode: block` and the row/table terminators need to be distinct so they nest cleanly.

!! The nesting problem

`TH`/`TD` markers in inline mode terminate at end-of-line, which is fine for one-line cells. For multi-line content you need ''block''-mode cell markers that terminate at the row terminator, while the row marker terminates at the table terminator. Three nesting levels need three distinct terminators.

!! Option 1: marker tiddlers (canonical, vocabulary-engine)

Re-use TABLE / ROW / CAPTION from [[Customize a Table]], and add two block-mode cell markers in the same `Vocab/Table` vocabulary:

|! Marker |! `open` |! `kind` |! `mode` |! `element` |! `end-string` |
|TABLE |`TABLE` |`word` |`block` |`table` |`---` |
|CAPTION |`CAPTION` |`word` |`inline` |`caption` | |
|ROW |`ROW` |`word` |`block` |`tr` |`--` |
|BLOCKTH |`BLOCKTH` |`word` |`block` |`th` |`||` |
|BLOCKTD |`BLOCKTD` |`word` |`block` |`td` |`||` |

The terminator pyramid is `---` for the table > `--` for rows > `||` for block cells. The block-cell terminator must be non-blank so blank lines can appear inside multi-paragraph cells.

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Table
```

Usage. Mix inline `TH`/`TD` with `BLOCKTH`/`BLOCKTD` per cell, using inline for one-line cells and block only where blank-line paragraph breaks are needed:

```
TABLE
CAPTION Superheros at a glance
ROW
TH Power
TH Batman
TH Flash
--
ROW
TH Skill
BLOCKTD Smarts. Plays chess. Reads books.

Has read the entire Library of Congress allegedly.
||
BLOCKTD Super speed. Vibrates through walls.

Time travel as a side effect.
||
--
---
```

Block-mode cells always wrap their body in a `<p>`, even when it's one line, which is wrong for short headers. Keep `BLOCKTH`/`BLOCKTD` for cells that genuinely need paragraph breaks. Each `BLOCKTD`/`BLOCKTH` consumes content up to its `||` terminator. `--` ends the row. `---` ends the table.

!! Option 2: inline pragma (escape hatch)

The same scheme with pragmas, scoped to a single tiddler. Activate Vocab/Legacy-Glyphs:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Legacy-Glyphs
```

Pragmas:

```
\custom tick=table   _element=table _mode=block _endString="---"
\custom tick=caption _element=caption
\custom tick=row     _element=tr    _mode=block _endString="--"
\custom tick=th      _element=th    _mode=block _classes=".hl"
\custom tick         _element=td    _mode=block _classes=".hl"
\custom angle        _element=td    _mode=block _classes=".hl"

´table ´caption Some caption text
´row
´th header 1
´th header 2
´th header 3
--
´row
» 1 text

» cell 12 text

» cell 13 text
line 2
line 3
--
---
```

Note the two different cell markers (`´` for short, `»` for long). They are separate registrations of the same `td` element. Use whichever reads cleanest in a given row.

A worked example lives at [[Example - TABLE with multiline cells]].

See [[Vocabulary Engine]] for the marker-field schema and [[Custom Markup Definition]] for the full pragma parameter list.
